# CVE-2026-34040 — Moby daemon authorisation bypass
#
# github.com/docker/docker v28.5.2 is a transitive dependency pulled in by
# dhui/dktest (via golang-migrate test helpers). It is used exclusively as a
# client SDK to communicate with a local Docker daemon during integration tests
# (testcontainers); the application never runs a Docker daemon itself.
#
# The vulnerability is in the daemon's authorisation layer, not in client-side
# code. Docker / Moby split the module path at v25: the fix ships as
# github.com/moby/moby/api v1.54.2+ (already our transitive dep via
# testcontainers-go v0.43.0), but dhui/dktest has not yet migrated and pins
# github.com/docker/docker v28.x, making an in-place upgrade impossible.
#
# Risk: none — the vulnerable code path is not reachable from a client-only
# consumer. Suppress until dhui/dktest drops the docker/docker dependency.
CVE-2026-34040
